fund-js/04-this-call-apply-bind/01-bind-.explanation:
Loop over the names, check the type, and assign the bound copy back onto the object:

```js
for (const name of names) {
  if (typeof obj[name] !== 'function') throw new TypeError(`${name} is not a function`);
  obj[name] = obj[name].bind(obj);
}
return obj;
```

Assigning the bound function as an OWN property shadows the prototype method, so it works for class instances too.

